# F2 v3 — Delta Against `f2-zustand-store-design.md` (v2)

**Document ID:** F2-DELTA-v3
**Type:** Change record — not a standalone document; read alongside F2 v2 (`f2-zustand-store-design.md`)
**Status:** ACCEPTED — all five items resolved; this delta is final pending re-merge into F2 v3 standalone
**Date:** 2026-06-19
**Direct cause:** Resolution of all five "Still open" items in F2 v2 §18, via ADR-012 through ADR-016
**Audience:** Frontend development team

---

## Summary

F2 v2 §18 listed five "Still open" items. All five are now resolved:

| # | Item | Resolution | ADR |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `roleCodes` shape in login response | `AuthResponseSchema` extended to return `roleCodes: string[]` (and `officeScopeId`, `officeCode`) directly; no second call | [ADR-012](./ADR-012-session-store-rolecodes-shape.md) |
| 3 | CERTIFICATION_OF_URGENCY / DOCUMENT_REQUEST_FORM in Step 1 picker | Both excluded from the generic picker; reachable only via dedicated entry points (`LOG_CERTIFICATION_OF_URGENCY` modal; `useDocumentRequestIntakeStore`) | [ADR-013](./ADR-013-document-intake-picker-scope.md) |
| 4 | Partial batch failure UX for Order of Business save | Sequential per-item commit, failed items stay in buffer and are highlighted, no rollback | [ADR-014](./ADR-014-order-of-business-batch-save-error-handling.md) |
| 5 | SSE reconnection / missed notification events | Native `EventSource` + server-side `Last-Event-ID` replay, plus unconditional TanStack Query refetch on drawer open as backstop | [ADR-015](./ADR-015-sse-reconnection-strategy.md) |
| 6 | Designation-substitute procedure name; `committeeId` strip test coverage | Confirmed as `organization.getActiveDesignations` (unscoped — client-side filter required); strip-before-send Vitest case made an explicit required test | [ADR-016](./ADR-016-designation-lookup-procedure-and-test-coverage.md) |

No store gains or loses a state field as a result of this delta, with one exception: none of the five items required a `DocumentIntakeState`/`SessionState`/`AttendanceState`/`OrderOfBusinessState`/`NotificationDrawerState` shape change at all. Every resolution either confirms an existing shape was already correct (items 1, 6-procedure-name) or adds usage-note-level orchestration detail and scope clarification that lives in components/hooks per F2's existing store/component boundary (items 3, 4, 5, 6-test-coverage). This is a low-risk delta.

