## Change 6 — §18 Known Gaps and Open Questions (full table restructure)

**Replace** the "### Still open" table in full. All five rows move to a "Resolved in this revision" table (joining the existing one from v2, which already held the ADR-007 resolution). No "Still open" table is needed unless new gaps are identified in a future revision; one new, smaller follow-up item is introduced by ADR-016 (the `positionTitle` literal-string confirmation) and is tracked below as the sole remaining open item.

**New §18 content (full replacement of both tables and the lead-in sentence):**

> `[Confirmed — ADR-012 through ADR-016]` All five items retained as "Still open" in F2 v2 are resolved in this revision. Combined with the prior resolution of item 2 (ADR-007), F2 v3 carries zero open items inherited from v1/v2. One new, narrower follow-up is introduced by ADR-016's resolution of item 6 and is tracked below.
>
> ### Resolved in this revision (and carried forward from v2)
>
> | # | Gap (as originally identified) | Resolution | ADR |
> |---|---|---|---|
> | 1 | `useSessionStore` must hold `roleCodes` for synchronous ABAC checks; login response shape (flat `string[]` vs. full `RoleAssignmentSelectSchema[]`) was unconfirmed. | `AuthResponseSchema` extended to return `roleCodes: string[]`, `officeScopeId`, `officeCode` directly, computed server-side at login. No second call; no store shape change. | [ADR-012](./ADR-012-session-store-rolecodes-shape.md) |
> | 2 (orig.) | The Phase 1B Designation document type tension in `useAttendanceStore` (presiding-officer substitute field deferred pending Designation reaching Phase 1). | Designation pulled into Phase 1; `presidingOfficerSubstituteId` modeled directly. | [ADR-007](./ADR-007-designation-document-type-phase1.md), [ADR-011](./ADR-011-f2-propagation-of-f1-adrs.md) |
> | 3 | Whether CERTIFICATION_OF_URGENCY and DOCUMENT_REQUEST_FORM appear in the Step 1 document-type picker needed a product decision. | Both excluded; each is created only through its own dedicated entry point (`LOG_CERTIFICATION_OF_URGENCY` modal; `useDocumentRequestIntakeStore`). | [ADR-013](./ADR-013-document-intake-picker-scope.md) |
> | 4 | Partial batch-failure UX for `useOrderOfBusinessStore.pendingChanges` was not detailed in any source document. | Sequential per-item commit; failed items remain in the buffer, highlighted, and retryable; no rollback of prior successes. | [ADR-014](./ADR-014-order-of-business-batch-save-error-handling.md) |
> | 5 | SSE reconnection strategy for `useNotificationDrawerStore.newArrivalCount` was not described in any source document. | Native `EventSource` reconnect + server-side `Last-Event-ID` replay as primary mechanism; unconditional TanStack Query refetch on drawer open as a correctness backstop; no continuous background poll added. | [ADR-015](./ADR-015-sse-reconnection-strategy.md) |
> | 6 | Procedure name for the presiding-officer-substitute lookup was unconfirmed; `committeeId` strip-before-send convention lacked specified test coverage. | Confirmed as `organization.getActiveDesignations` (unscoped — client-side filter by `positionTitle` + date range required). Strip-before-send Vitest case added as an explicit required test in §17. | [ADR-016](./ADR-016-designation-lookup-procedure-and-test-coverage.md) |
>
> ### Still open
>
> | # | Gap / question | Where it surfaces | Status |
> |---|---|---|---|
> | 7 | The literal display string for the SP Presiding Officer `positionTitle` value returned by `organization.getActiveDesignations` (e.g. `"Vice Mayor"`, `"Presiding Officer"`, or something else) is not confirmed against actual `organization.positions` seed data. `useAttendanceStore`'s client-side filter (§14, per ADR-016) cannot be implemented exactly until this string is confirmed. | §14 `useAttendanceStore` | `[Unverified]` — narrower in scope than the original item 6; raised by ADR-016 as a direct consequence of resolving it |

---

## Net Effect

- **Zero state-shape changes** across all eleven stores. Every resolution either confirmed an existing design (items 1, 6-procedure) or added usage-note/testing-guidance detail that was always going to live outside the store's TypeScript interfaces (items 3, 4, 5, 6-test).
- **One backend-facing action item** falls out of this delta: E3's `AuthResponseSchema` must be updated per ADR-012 before `/web`'s login flow can be implemented exactly as F2 §5 already specifies.
- **One new, smaller open item** (positionTitle literal string) replaces the closed item 6, to be resolved by checking `organization.positions` seed data — a data-lookup task, not a design question.

This delta, applied to F2 v2, constitutes F2 v3. Given the small surface area of the actual changes (five usage-note-level insertions/replacements plus one table restructure, zero interface changes), the team may choose to apply this delta as a tracked diff against the existing `f2-zustand-store-design.md` file rather than regenerating a new ~1000-line standalone document; both are equivalent in content. If a standalone F2 v3 is regenerated for a future revision with more substantial changes, this delta's six change blocks are what must be folded in.